1
00:00:00,759 --> 00:00:03,383
(suspenseful music)

2
00:00:09,924 --> 00:00:10,966
I mean it.

3
00:00:11,924 --> 00:00:12,299
I'm going.

4
00:00:12,382 --> 00:00:14,631
No, you're not.

5
00:00:14,715 --> 00:00:16,423
Because, as I've
already explained,

6
00:00:18,547 --> 00:00:19,297
if a veil has been cast,

7
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:21,672
then there is a
strong likelihood

8
00:00:21,755 --> 00:00:22,839
that he's still alive,

9
00:00:22,922 --> 00:00:24,963
and he's there at
Satozakura High School.

10
00:00:29,088 --> 00:00:30,628
I'll be back soon.

11
00:00:30,712 --> 00:00:33,129
I'm ordering you to
wait there for me, Itadori.

12
00:00:35,419 --> 00:00:38,794
It was probably pointless
to even ask him that.

13
00:00:39,544 --> 00:00:44,085
As you heard, I need to go,
so I'll leave this to you, Ino.

14
00:00:44,169 --> 00:00:45,210
What?

15
00:00:46,250 --> 00:00:47,375
Why, is that a problem?

16
00:00:47,459 --> 00:00:50,209
Well, um, it's just, um,

17
00:00:51,958 --> 00:00:53,332
there's a lot of 'em,

18
00:00:53,416 --> 00:00:56,249
and I think they're all humans.

19
00:00:56,332 --> 00:00:58,248
I was thinking of
recommending you for promotion

20
00:00:58,331 --> 00:01:00,999
to grade one sorcerer.

21
00:01:02,414 --> 00:01:04,497
(Ino grunts)

22
00:01:04,581 --> 00:01:09,413
All right, let's get this
done, baby! Ha ha!

23
00:01:09,496 --> 00:01:12,496
(suspenseful music continues)

24
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:14,370
[Itadori] Please
step aside Ijichi.

25
00:01:15,579 --> 00:01:18,494
Don't forget that our
job is to help others.

26
00:01:18,578 --> 00:01:20,870
And though you're a student,

27
00:01:20,953 --> 00:01:22,828
that includes even you, Itadori.

28
00:01:24,994 --> 00:01:27,077
I'm not about to make
any more mistakes.

29
00:01:30,034 --> 00:01:32,576
You mustn't go there, Itadori.

30
00:01:36,283 --> 00:01:37,283
I'm sorry, Ijichi.

31
00:01:37,366 --> 00:01:42,199
(suspenseful music continues)

32
00:01:46,157 --> 00:01:48,823
What are you
doing? Stop, Junpei!

33
00:01:50,073 --> 00:01:51,530
(lightning crashes)

34
00:01:51,613 --> 00:01:53,405
Jujutsu sorcerer, back off.

35
00:02:00,155 --> 00:02:02,653
(Opening Theme Music)

36
00:02:16,026 --> 00:02:19,400
(man singing in Japanese)

37
00:03:26,513 --> 00:03:29,554
(suspenseful music)

38
00:03:33,554 --> 00:03:35,803
(Junpei panting)

39
00:03:35,886 --> 00:03:36,803
(Itadori grunts)

40
00:03:36,886 --> 00:03:38,678
[Junpei] Moon Dregs!

41
00:03:44,094 --> 00:03:46,009
[Itadori] A jellyfish shikigami?

42
00:03:46,093 --> 00:03:48,884
Blunt attacks won't even
touch him when he's inside that!

43
00:03:50,592 --> 00:03:52,050
I'll say it one more time.

44
00:03:52,134 --> 00:03:54,800
Stay out of this,
jujutsu sorcerer.

45
00:03:54,883 --> 00:03:56,341
It's none of your business.

46
00:03:56,591 --> 00:03:59,465
You don't tell me
what my business is!

47
00:04:00,924 --> 00:04:03,381
What's the point, really,
of saving indiscriminately?

48
00:04:03,464 --> 00:04:05,840
(Junpei grunts)

49
00:04:05,923 --> 00:04:08,005
Don't overestimate

50
00:04:08,089 --> 00:04:09,839
the value of a life!

51
00:04:09,922 --> 00:04:11,672
(tentacles whipping)

52
00:04:11,755 --> 00:04:13,462
(Itadori groans)

53
00:04:13,546 --> 00:04:16,587
People always pretend
their emotions are everything,

54
00:04:16,671 --> 00:04:19,420
but the heart is just the
metabolism of the soul.

55
00:04:19,503 --> 00:04:21,878
It's all a delusion.

56
00:04:21,962 --> 00:04:25,128
Don't restrict me with rules
that are based on a delusion.

57
00:04:25,961 --> 00:04:27,086
What gives anyone the right

58
00:04:27,169 --> 00:04:29,044
to stop someone
from taking a life?

59
00:04:29,128 --> 00:04:30,876
Nothing does.

60
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:32,501
Now, just go sleep over there.

61
00:04:32,584 --> 00:04:35,542
There's something I
have to go back and do.

62
00:04:36,583 --> 00:04:39,208
(Junpei groans)

63
00:04:39,291 --> 00:04:42,332
Your cursed technique is poison.

64
00:04:43,666 --> 00:04:46,124
You produce poison
from cursed energy,

65
00:04:46,206 --> 00:04:48,581
and then your
shikigami secretes it.

66
00:04:48,665 --> 00:04:50,206
Soon you will learn

67
00:04:50,289 --> 00:04:52,872
how to control their
size and their strength,

68
00:04:52,956 --> 00:04:54,247
and that of the poison.

69
00:04:54,664 --> 00:04:58,496
A normal jujutsu sorcerer
would need some time to grasp it,

70
00:04:58,579 --> 00:05:00,913
but I'll teach you the sensation

71
00:05:00,996 --> 00:05:02,954
so you'll be able
to fight right away.

72
00:05:04,453 --> 00:05:05,578
Junpei, you have talent.

73
00:05:09,994 --> 00:05:11,834
[Itadori] Who were you
trying to convince here?

74
00:05:16,701 --> 00:05:18,660
(Itadori grunts)

75
00:05:20,826 --> 00:05:23,617
(blows thudding)

76
00:05:25,783 --> 00:05:29,075
(Itadori grunts)

77
00:05:29,158 --> 00:05:30,907
(Itadori yells)

78
00:05:30,990 --> 00:05:33,281
(Junpei groans)

79
00:05:33,365 --> 00:05:38,406
[Junpei] Why, why doesn't
Moon Dregs' poison work on him?

80
00:05:39,489 --> 00:05:42,613
-(shikigami thudding)
-(Junpei groaning)

81
00:05:44,863 --> 00:05:47,779
Why are you getting
in my way? Why?

82
00:05:48,654 --> 00:05:49,737
Why?

83
00:05:49,821 --> 00:05:51,945
(blood splattering)

84
00:05:52,028 --> 00:05:53,070
Why?

85
00:05:53,986 --> 00:05:56,778
(Junpei grunting)

86
00:05:58,568 --> 00:06:02,111
He's in the air,
so he can't dodge,

87
00:06:02,193 --> 00:06:05,609
and now I have a chance to
crush him just before he lands.

88
00:06:06,651 --> 00:06:09,608
(Itadori grunting)

89
00:06:10,817 --> 00:06:12,608
(Itadori yells)

90
00:06:12,691 --> 00:06:14,607
(Junpei groans)

91
00:06:14,690 --> 00:06:17,649
Junpei, I really
can't understand

92
00:06:18,857 --> 00:06:21,648
a single thing you're saying.

93
00:06:23,272 --> 00:06:25,688
String together
whatever logic you want.

94
00:06:26,897 --> 00:06:30,063
With shikigami, strike
the sorcerer directly.

95
00:06:30,646 --> 00:06:32,896
But all you're doing is

96
00:06:36,269 --> 00:06:37,603
trying to convince yourself

97
00:06:37,686 --> 00:06:40,145
you're on the
right side of this.

98
00:06:40,228 --> 00:06:44,602
-(punch booming)
-(glass shattering)

99
00:06:44,685 --> 00:06:47,309
Even though I don't
know why you're doing this,

100
00:06:47,393 --> 00:06:49,935
I'll assume you have
a good reason for it.

101
00:06:50,018 --> 00:06:51,767
But whatever it is,

102
00:06:51,850 --> 00:06:54,142
(melancholy music)

103
00:06:54,225 --> 00:06:56,892
is it really worth throwing
away the life that you have?

104
00:06:58,265 --> 00:06:59,557
(Junpei sobbing)

105
00:06:59,641 --> 00:07:01,001
The human heart
is just a delusion?

106
00:07:01,891 --> 00:07:04,848
Could you really say
that in front of her?

107
00:07:05,890 --> 00:07:09,472
[Junpei] People
don't have hearts.

108
00:07:09,555 --> 00:07:11,075
-You're still just
trying- -They don't!

109
00:07:13,263 --> 00:07:16,013
Otherwise...

110
00:07:16,097 --> 00:07:17,179
Otherwise...

111
00:07:17,262 --> 00:07:19,720
And that could only mean

112
00:07:19,804 --> 00:07:22,845
that people cursed me and
my mom with those hearts.

113
00:07:23,804 --> 00:07:26,844
That would just be too much.

114
00:07:28,260 --> 00:07:30,343
Then I, I wouldn't even know

115
00:07:31,468 --> 00:07:33,094
what is right and
what's wrong anymore.

116
00:07:36,258 --> 00:07:37,801
(tentacles whipping)

117
00:07:37,884 --> 00:07:42,050
(flesh squelching)

118
00:07:42,133 --> 00:07:42,716
(melancholy music)

119
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:46,008
(Itadori groans)

120
00:07:46,092 --> 00:07:48,091
Why didn't you dodge it?

121
00:07:52,464 --> 00:07:53,714
I'm sorry.

122
00:07:53,798 --> 00:07:54,589
I said a lot of arrogant stuff

123
00:07:54,672 --> 00:07:58,089
without really
understanding anything.

124
00:08:02,505 --> 00:08:07,046
So, tell me what happened
to you, and I swear to you,

125
00:08:07,129 --> 00:08:08,768
if you do, then I won't
curse you anymore.

126
00:08:10,961 --> 00:08:12,378
Please.

127
00:08:12,461 --> 00:08:16,168
(melancholy music continues)

128
00:08:20,334 --> 00:08:21,334
No way.

129
00:08:21,376 --> 00:08:22,417
Your mom.

130
00:08:28,416 --> 00:08:30,999
Junpei, join Jujutsu Tech.

131
00:08:32,165 --> 00:08:33,083
You'd like it.

132
00:08:33,165 --> 00:08:34,725
There are lots of
crazy strong teachers,

133
00:08:34,791 --> 00:08:37,206
and good, reliable
friends there.

134
00:08:37,956 --> 00:08:40,748
If we all work together,
I guarantee you,

135
00:08:40,831 --> 00:08:44,747
we can find whoever it
was that cursed your mom.

136
00:08:44,830 --> 00:08:47,371
Then you can make them
pay for what they did.

137
00:08:48,496 --> 00:08:49,496
Let's fight together!

138
00:08:53,495 --> 00:08:54,411
Huh?

139
00:08:54,495 --> 00:08:55,536
(Mahito chuckles)

140
00:08:55,620 --> 00:08:56,620
Who are you?

141
00:08:58,119 --> 00:08:59,119
Who the hell's this?

142
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:03,118
Is it a person?

143
00:09:03,201 --> 00:09:04,201
It's nice to meet you.

144
00:09:04,826 --> 00:09:08,325
[Itadori] No, this feels like...

145
00:09:08,408 --> 00:09:09,950
Vessel of Sukuna.

146
00:09:11,909 --> 00:09:13,949
Mahito, no! Don't do it!

147
00:09:14,033 --> 00:09:18,282
-(impact thudding)
-(Itadori groaning)

148
00:09:18,366 --> 00:09:19,365
What am I, an idiot?

149
00:09:19,448 --> 00:09:22,573
A human-shaped cursed
spirit with a patchwork face?

150
00:09:22,656 --> 00:09:25,073
This is exactly what Nanami
told me would happen!

151
00:09:25,155 --> 00:09:26,364
Junpei, get out!

152
00:09:27,655 --> 00:09:28,840
I don't care what your
relationship is with him.

153
00:09:28,864 --> 00:09:33,237
Right now, just get
your ass outta here. Run!

154
00:09:34,363 --> 00:09:35,653
Itadori, calm down.

155
00:09:35,737 --> 00:09:39,112
Mahito's not a bad person.

156
00:09:39,195 --> 00:09:40,570
Huh?

157
00:09:40,653 --> 00:09:44,778
(mysterious voices singing)

158
00:09:44,861 --> 00:09:45,944
Bad person.

159
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:50,818
(brooding music)

160
00:09:50,902 --> 00:09:55,192
You know, Junpei, you
are a pretty smart kid.

161
00:09:55,901 --> 00:09:57,816
But sometimes, thinking
too much can lead

162
00:09:57,900 --> 00:10:02,358
to even more foolish
decisions than impulsiveness.

163
00:10:02,441 --> 00:10:04,482
You're a classic case of that.

164
00:10:05,024 --> 00:10:09,481
I'd even say that you can
actually be almost as foolish

165
00:10:09,564 --> 00:10:11,856
as those people you
call fools yourself.

166
00:10:14,396 --> 00:10:16,271
And that's why you'll die.

167
00:10:18,188 --> 00:10:19,188
Idle Transfiguration.

168
00:10:19,896 --> 00:10:23,771
(Junpei groaning)

169
00:10:23,854 --> 00:10:27,519
(dramatic music)

170
00:10:28,811 --> 00:10:29,853
Now,

171
00:10:31,477 --> 00:10:32,977
time for round two.

172
00:10:33,061 --> 00:10:34,061
(Junpei growls)

173
00:10:34,102 --> 00:10:35,352
Junpei.

174
00:10:35,435 --> 00:10:37,642
-(punch thwacking)
-(Itadori groans)

175
00:10:37,726 --> 00:10:39,018
Junpei!

176
00:10:39,101 --> 00:10:41,183
Get ahold of yourself!

177
00:10:41,266 --> 00:10:42,641
I can heal you!

178
00:10:45,475 --> 00:10:48,891
(punches thudding)

179
00:10:48,974 --> 00:10:50,016
Sukuna.

180
00:10:51,265 --> 00:10:52,264
Sukuna!

181
00:10:54,723 --> 00:10:55,639
What now?

182
00:10:55,723 --> 00:10:56,639
(Mahito giggles)

183
00:10:56,723 --> 00:10:57,638
I'll do anything.

184
00:10:57,722 --> 00:10:59,889
I'll let you do whatever
you wanna do to me,

185
00:10:59,972 --> 00:11:01,823
and all agree to any twisted
thing you come up with

186
00:11:01,847 --> 00:11:04,137
if you heal Junpei,

187
00:11:04,220 --> 00:11:06,971
like you did when
you restored my heart.

188
00:11:07,055 --> 00:11:09,928
I refuse to. (laughs)

189
00:11:11,928 --> 00:11:12,928
Oh.

190
00:11:13,678 --> 00:11:14,594
[Itadori] Damn you!

191
00:11:14,677 --> 00:11:17,844
(Sukuna laughs)

192
00:11:17,927 --> 00:11:21,885
Excellent. He's completely
forgotten about that pact.

193
00:11:24,134 --> 00:11:24,759
How very amusing.

194
00:11:24,842 --> 00:11:26,925
You're offering your pride,

195
00:11:27,009 --> 00:11:28,592
your future, and
your everything,

196
00:11:28,675 --> 00:11:33,215
all just to grovel and beg
me for my help. (laughs)

197
00:11:33,299 --> 00:11:36,214
By yourself, you
can't save anyone.

198
00:11:36,298 --> 00:11:39,381
[Mahito] Is Sukuna
refusing the kid's pact?

199
00:11:39,465 --> 00:11:41,049
The shape of one's
soul isn't something

200
00:11:41,131 --> 00:11:45,048
that reverse-cursed
techniques could deal with, so,

201
00:11:45,130 --> 00:11:48,379
maybe healing
others is beyond him?

202
00:11:48,463 --> 00:11:49,546
How pitiful.

203
00:11:49,629 --> 00:11:52,047
You couldn't be any more
pathetic, you sorry little punk.

204
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:53,920
(Sukuna laughs)

205
00:11:54,004 --> 00:11:56,253
[Mahito] Although,
what I'm really after

206
00:11:56,337 --> 00:11:57,211
is what comes next,

207
00:11:57,295 --> 00:12:01,961
so I guess this will
do just fine. (laughs)

208
00:12:03,501 --> 00:12:06,960
(dramatic music continues)

209
00:12:10,167 --> 00:12:12,001
(Sukuna laughs)

210
00:12:18,166 --> 00:12:20,082
[Itadori] Oh, that's right.

211
00:12:20,165 --> 00:12:24,956
At the end of the day,
both of these two are curses.

212
00:12:34,371 --> 00:12:35,829
[Junpei] Yuuji.

213
00:12:41,911 --> 00:12:43,453
Help

214
00:12:43,536 --> 00:12:44,536
me.

215
00:12:50,994 --> 00:12:53,035
(body thudding)

216
00:12:53,117 --> 00:12:56,826
(dramatic music continues)

217
00:13:01,992 --> 00:13:04,824
(Mahito laughs)

218
00:13:11,531 --> 00:13:12,865
Oh, dead already?

219
00:13:12,948 --> 00:13:16,947
I was kind of rough when I
changed his shape, I'll admit.

220
00:13:18,947 --> 00:13:21,154
That's how it goes.

221
00:13:21,237 --> 00:13:23,071
(punch booming)

222
00:13:25,194 --> 00:13:28,111
That was an unusual
blow. Interesting.

223
00:13:28,194 --> 00:13:30,694
But sorry to say,
that won't work,

224
00:13:30,777 --> 00:13:33,485
so long as I maintain
the shape of my...

225
00:13:33,569 --> 00:13:34,610
Oh!

226
00:13:37,401 --> 00:13:38,443
What's going on?

227
00:13:39,568 --> 00:13:43,567
He struck the shape of my
soul, as well as my body?

228
00:13:45,734 --> 00:13:47,107
Oh, that's right.

229
00:13:47,190 --> 00:13:49,941
Yuuji Itadori is a vessel.

230
00:13:50,025 --> 00:13:51,941
His body constantly
houses another soul

231
00:13:52,025 --> 00:13:55,189
in addition to his own.

232
00:13:55,273 --> 00:13:56,857
So, naturally...

233
00:13:58,147 --> 00:14:02,689
You are actually aware
of the outline of your soul?

234
00:14:10,270 --> 00:14:13,145
[Itadori] The next words
that spilled from my lips

235
00:14:13,228 --> 00:14:15,978
came from so deep within my gut

236
00:14:16,061 --> 00:14:17,519
that it nearly made everything

237
00:14:17,602 --> 00:14:19,020
I've ever said feel like a lie.

238
00:14:21,143 --> 00:14:22,810
I will kill you!

239
00:14:28,767 --> 00:14:31,266
(upbeat music)

240
00:14:42,431 --> 00:14:47,305
Don't you mean you'll
exorcize me, jujutsu sorcerer?

241
00:14:47,388 --> 00:14:50,014
(Mahito slurps)

242
00:14:50,096 --> 00:14:53,054
Yuuji Itadori isn't
concerned with his own life.

243
00:14:54,429 --> 00:14:56,387
But Getou forbade
me from forcing him

244
00:14:56,470 --> 00:14:58,136
into an external
pact using a hostages.

245
00:14:59,720 --> 00:15:03,177
So, if he has a foe he hates
so much, he longs to kill them,

246
00:15:03,260 --> 00:15:06,510
but he still can't, he'll
probably turn to Sukuna.

247
00:15:07,927 --> 00:15:09,217
If Junpei pay isn't enough

248
00:15:09,301 --> 00:15:11,175
then I'll have to
transform every student,

249
00:15:11,259 --> 00:15:14,216
one by one,
before his very eyes.

250
00:15:14,300 --> 00:15:15,842
That would push Itadori,

251
00:15:15,925 --> 00:15:18,675
while he's all full of
hatred and self-interest,

252
00:15:18,758 --> 00:15:21,049
to negotiate and forge
a pact with Sukuna.

253
00:15:21,132 --> 00:15:23,590
If that also
improves the chances

254
00:15:23,674 --> 00:15:28,381
of Sukuna joining our side,
then all the better. (slurps)

255
00:15:28,464 --> 00:15:29,214
(dramatic music)

256
00:15:29,298 --> 00:15:31,213
Though, all of that presumes

257
00:15:31,297 --> 00:15:34,047
that I really am
stronger than him.

258
00:15:34,297 --> 00:15:36,963
So, why did he have to be

259
00:15:37,046 --> 00:15:40,046
my natural enemy?

260
00:15:40,129 --> 00:15:42,086
(Itadori growls)

261
00:15:43,128 --> 00:15:46,712
(Itadori yells)

262
00:15:55,835 --> 00:15:58,042
(Mahito giggles)

263
00:15:58,125 --> 00:16:00,250
[Itadori] He keeps
changing his damn shape!

264
00:16:00,333 --> 00:16:02,001
I'd better stop using combos

265
00:16:02,083 --> 00:16:05,416
and start using throwing
techniques instead.

266
00:16:05,499 --> 00:16:07,916
[Mahito] Now that I know
his attacks work on me,

267
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,415
changing my shape and giving him

268
00:16:09,498 --> 00:16:11,581
a bigger target is a bad idea.

269
00:16:12,206 --> 00:16:14,664
[Both] In that case.

270
00:16:14,747 --> 00:16:17,998
[Itadori] Even if it takes 100
times, or even 1,000 times,

271
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:20,204
I'm just going to
keep on pounding him

272
00:16:21,204 --> 00:16:23,997
until I pound them into a pulp!

273
00:16:24,079 --> 00:16:28,662
[Mahito] I'll use a shape
more refined toward murder,

274
00:16:28,745 --> 00:16:31,786
with more
inspiration for murder,

275
00:16:32,869 --> 00:16:34,077
and manifest it!

276
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:39,910
-(dramatic music)
-(Mahito roars)

277
00:16:40,743 --> 00:16:43,742
(explosion booming)

278
00:16:50,241 --> 00:16:54,323
(Mahito laughs)

279
00:16:54,407 --> 00:16:57,115
(Itadori groans)

280
00:16:59,239 --> 00:17:02,239
There's no way your limbs
can keep on stretching forever.

281
00:17:05,154 --> 00:17:06,947
(flesh squelching)

282
00:17:07,030 --> 00:17:08,280
(Itadori groans)

283
00:17:08,363 --> 00:17:10,279
(dramatic music continues)

284
00:17:10,362 --> 00:17:13,946
(Itadori roars)

285
00:17:20,110 --> 00:17:24,777
[Mahito] You know, most
people would've just let go.

286
00:17:24,860 --> 00:17:26,526
Spreading my shape
too much causes it

287
00:17:26,609 --> 00:17:28,651
to lose strength
and maneuverability.

288
00:17:29,567 --> 00:17:30,858
(Itadori yells)

289
00:17:30,942 --> 00:17:33,566
(punch booming)

290
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:38,190
(Mahito giggles)

291
00:17:38,274 --> 00:17:43,856
-(Itadori grunts)
-(punches booming)

292
00:17:43,940 --> 00:17:46,815
(flesh squelching)

293
00:17:47,272 --> 00:17:50,730
(brooding music)

294
00:17:50,814 --> 00:17:52,980
(flesh squelching)

295
00:17:53,062 --> 00:17:56,854
Ah, you can never
beat me, you know,

296
00:17:56,938 --> 00:17:58,979
so swap out already.

297
00:17:59,061 --> 00:18:00,144
(Itadori groans)

298
00:18:00,228 --> 00:18:01,228
With Sukuna.

299
00:18:03,769 --> 00:18:06,019
Idle Transfiguration.

300
00:18:13,810 --> 00:18:16,934
You dare to actually
touch my soul?

301
00:18:17,017 --> 00:18:19,225
Since both of us heartily
ridiculed that brat before,

302
00:18:19,308 --> 00:18:22,557
I'll allow it this once.

303
00:18:22,641 --> 00:18:25,266
There won't be a second time.

304
00:18:27,431 --> 00:18:30,390
Don't forget your place.

305
00:18:32,014 --> 00:18:33,014
Foolish puppet.

306
00:18:39,346 --> 00:18:41,304
I'm not swapping out.

307
00:18:41,388 --> 00:18:42,887
I already told you.

308
00:18:45,095 --> 00:18:49,427
For what you did, I
will kill you now. (roars)

309
00:18:49,511 --> 00:18:51,302
(headbutt booming)

310
00:18:51,386 --> 00:18:54,510
(headbutts thudding)

311
00:18:58,010 --> 00:19:01,050
(blood splattering)

312
00:19:03,675 --> 00:19:06,216
(kick booming)

313
00:19:12,674 --> 00:19:15,256
(Itadori yells)

314
00:19:22,880 --> 00:19:23,922
Huh?

315
00:19:26,504 --> 00:19:29,254
(blade clanking)

316
00:19:30,379 --> 00:19:31,378
Ha.

317
00:19:32,336 --> 00:19:33,336
Uh?

318
00:19:35,253 --> 00:19:36,961
Nanami?

319
00:19:37,043 --> 00:19:39,543
(Nanami sighs)

320
00:19:40,377 --> 00:19:44,334
I'll lecture you later.
Just tell me the situation.

321
00:19:46,668 --> 00:19:49,500
Two died. I failed to save them.

322
00:19:50,917 --> 00:19:53,791
Why is he always
thinking of others first?

323
00:19:53,874 --> 00:19:56,249
I want to hear about
your physical condition.

324
00:19:56,332 --> 00:20:01,122
I'm fine, thanks. Though,
I am kinda full of holes.

325
00:20:02,081 --> 00:20:03,789
That's not fine.

326
00:20:03,872 --> 00:20:05,622
Also, in the school gym,

327
00:20:05,705 --> 00:20:08,580
the students are
alive, but unconscious.

328
00:20:08,664 --> 00:20:13,496
My, my, so you're alive
and well, Mr. Seven-to-Three.

329
00:20:13,579 --> 00:20:16,828
Good to see both of us survived.

330
00:20:16,912 --> 00:20:21,494
Shall we share a little hug
in celebration of our reunion?

331
00:20:21,577 --> 00:20:24,535
(suspenseful music)

332
00:20:27,451 --> 00:20:29,326
[Nanami] Itadori, why
is his nose bleeding?

333
00:20:29,409 --> 00:20:32,367
Uh, I smashed his face in?

334
00:20:32,450 --> 00:20:33,367
But when?

335
00:20:33,450 --> 00:20:35,659
At the start of the fight.

336
00:20:35,742 --> 00:20:36,861
And did his hands touch you?

337
00:20:37,407 --> 00:20:39,824
Mm-hmm.

338
00:20:39,908 --> 00:20:41,508
[Nanami] My attacks
aren't going to work on him.

339
00:20:41,532 --> 00:20:42,448
Huh?

340
00:20:42,531 --> 00:20:44,823
Wait, what? But why not?

341
00:20:44,907 --> 00:20:47,198
I'll explain it later,
when I'm lecturing you.

342
00:20:47,281 --> 00:20:48,989
It's either because, one,

343
00:20:49,072 --> 00:20:51,530
his technique doesn't
work on Itadori,

344
00:20:51,614 --> 00:20:55,238
or two, there's some
reason he won't kill Itadori.

345
00:20:55,321 --> 00:20:57,488
Either way, it's good for us.

346
00:20:57,571 --> 00:21:00,153
However, I'll try to keep
him from moving around.

347
00:21:01,779 --> 00:21:03,861
Then, once we
both got an opening,

348
00:21:03,945 --> 00:21:05,569
we'll shower him with blows.

349
00:21:07,110 --> 00:21:09,318
We'll exorcize this
one here and now.

350
00:21:11,443 --> 00:21:12,443
Yeah!

351
00:21:15,609 --> 00:21:20,608
(Closing Theme Music)

352
00:22:45,635 --> 00:22:47,592
-(whimsical music)
-(voices moaning)

353
00:22:47,675 --> 00:22:50,467
(whimsical music)

354
00:22:54,633 --> 00:22:58,424
(creatures moaning)

355
00:23:02,506 --> 00:23:03,590
Oh, look.

356
00:23:03,673 --> 00:23:05,422
Huh?

357
00:23:07,339 --> 00:23:08,130
Ah!

358
00:23:08,214 --> 00:23:13,254
-Huh?
-(yellow man speaks gibberish)

359
00:23:17,587 --> 00:23:19,462
(object clicks)

360
00:23:21,419 --> 00:23:23,044
[Everyone] Huh?

361
00:23:25,211 --> 00:23:30,251
-(object clicking)
-(creatures grunting)

362
00:23:33,876 --> 00:23:36,667
-(pirate pops)
-Oh!

363
00:23:38,917 --> 00:23:41,958
(creatures yelling)

364
00:23:43,123 --> 00:23:45,165
(pirate clattering)

365
00:23:45,248 --> 00:23:47,915
(dramatic music)

